Passbolt CE on FenrirOS
=======================

Code: /usr/share/passbolt (config/ is /etc/passbolt, tmp/ is
/var/lib/passbolt/tmp, logs/ is /var/log/passbolt). PHP runs as _php
(php-fpm); its GnuPG home is /var/lib/passbolt/.gnupg.

1. Database: install mariadb (or postgresql), then
     CREATE DATABASE passbolt CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
     CREATE USER 'passbolt'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '<password>';
     GRANT ALL ON passbolt.* TO 'passbolt'@'localhost';
2. Server key (no passphrase; Passbolt needs it unattended), as _php:
     su -s /bin/sh _php -c 'HOME=/var/lib/passbolt gpg --batch --no-tty --gen-key' <<KEY
     Key-Type: RSA
     Key-Length: 3072
     Name-Real: Passbolt server
     Name-Email: passbolt@example.org
     Expire-Date: 0
     %no-protection
     %commit
     KEY
   then export it to /etc/passbolt/gpg/serverkey.asc and
   serverkey_private.asc (gpg --armor --export / --export-secret-keys).
3. cp /etc/passbolt/passbolt.default.php /etc/passbolt/passbolt.php and set
   App.fullBaseUrl, the database, email, the server key fingerprint, and
   'gpg' => ['keyring' => '/var/lib/passbolt/.gnupg'].
4. su -s /bin/sh _php -c 'HOME=/var/lib/passbolt /usr/share/passbolt/bin/cake passbolt install'
5. nginx: /usr/share/doc/passbolt/nginx-passbolt.conf; enable php-fpm and
   nginx. Email queue: cp /usr/share/doc/passbolt/passbolt.cron
   /etc/cron.d/passbolt and dinitctl enable crond.
